        "original_id": "8eeb8c9f-bc64-54fc-a95d-19cdc63ae7b3",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Robert Case\n- Events: 1991 Perfect Storm, 1991 Halloween blizzard\n- Places: Atlantic Canada, Atlantic Ocean, eastern United States, Gulf of Mexico\n\nFacts:\n- Over the last week of October 1991, the 1991 Perfect Storm over the Atlantic Ocean blocked most weather patterns over the eastern half of the United States.\n- Over the last week of October 1991, the 1991 Perfect Storm funneled moisture from the Gulf of Mexico straight northward over the region affected by the 1991 Halloween blizzard.\n- On October 29, 1991, the initial area of low pressure for the 1991 Perfect Storm developed off Atlantic Canada.\n- Robert Case is best known for inspiring the naming of the 1991 Perfect Storm as \"The Perfect Storm.\"",
